ParchaOS: file piles and the desktop menu (ticket #175)

Desktop files are grouped into piles by kind (Pictures, Screenshots, Screen
Recordings, Documents, ...), by a date (last opened, added, modified, created)
or by Parcher's colour tag, chosen under Sort Piles By. A pile is drawn as its
three newest files fanned; clicking opens it in place and clicking again closes
it. The desktop menu gains Properties, Change Wallpaper, Group Files into Piles,
Sort Piles By and Icon Options, and menu check marks follow settings changed
elsewhere. Builds on DING's own stacks (keep-stacked, unstackedtypes).

Original code for ParchaOS, GPL-3.0.

